In article <2742@ecs.soton.ac.uk> tjc@ecs.soton.ac.uk (Tim Chown) writes:
>Has anyone else got any tales of remarkable good fortune from
>nethack games?  Talk on this group tends to be about game
>improvements, rather than about games played.  The latter is
>a more common talking point amongst "hackers" here!

  I once had an amazing start to a game.  I was a wizard walking around
on the first level when I came upon a fountain.  I drank, and was rewarded
with a wish from a Water Demon.  I explored the level further, only to
find a wand of wishing sitting in the middle of a room.  Unfortunately,
I wasn't experienced enough to know all of the good wishes possible, and
I didn't know to wish for a blessed scroll of charging to get the most
out of my wand.
